\subsection{Extended thermo-hydraulic formulation}
%% <<KEEP:pressure-drop>> <<KEEP:temp-prop>> <<KEEP:delay>>
%% <<GAP:HYDRAULIC-DETAIL>> Answers R2.4. Supply AND return circuits; trunk pressure
%% drop (DW, L3); the differential-pressure requirement at the critical consumer and
%% its source (0.6 bar, real spec); pump characteristics and efficiency (Wilo IL-E
%% datasheets); resulting pump-energy share reconciled with the 1-5% literature by
%% network scale (compact, oversized pumps -> ~0.03%, validated against 110.8 kW
%% installed vs ~3 kW need and pandapipes <0.007 bar trunk agreement -- NOT inflated).

\subsubsection{Station-resolved hydraulics (L4, L5) -- NEW}
%% <<GAP:STATION-HYDRAULICS>> The demand side resolved to the individual transmission
%% station. L4 adds: (i) station count n_transfer_stations per node (174 real, from
%% DXF); (ii) service-lateral (last-mile) losses from real DXF trace lengths -- these
%% appear ONLY at L4, so coarser levels honestly undercount real loss and use
%% DEFENSIBLE trunk U (no x4.7 multiplier); (iii) flat per-station Dp. L5 replaces the
%% flat station Dp with a DYNAMIC flow-dependent Dp (convex PWL, no binaries) and the
%% associated station pumping. Validated on Memmingen real component data + pandapipes;
%% parameterised (stations ~ node demand, bootstrap laterals) for the synthetic
%% out-of-sample test. Headline: resolved to the station, hydraulics change cost by <1%
%% and decisions by ~0.
%% <<GAP:TRANSPORT-DELAY>> L6 isolates transport delay (linear time-shift). The
%% nonlinear reference (NL: bilinear temp-prop + quadratic DW) is NOT solved (global
%% MIQCP intractable -- 24h, no incumbent); linearisation error is bounded by exact
%% decomposition + the forward evaluator (answers R2.3).
\input{tables/tab_lplus_vs_lnl}   %% = unified Table 2 (08_LEVEL_REDESIGN.md)

